From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:43:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: hold the SoC rail up
 while the video engines work

On the 14-inch MacBook Pro M4 nothing raises the SoC rail while the
video decoder or encoder works: during a decode or an encode every PMC
agent's floor reads 0. The CLPC raises it only for CPU demand. With
the SoC rail held at state 3 (what the CLPC's T8132 table votes), the
decoder does H.264 1080p at 2389 fps instead of 1192 and VP9 1080p at
961 instead of 446. The encoder does HEVC 4K at 53.8 fps instead of
27.7 in its quality mode. macOS reaches 2702, 1011 and 59.6 fps.

As on the M4 Pro, describe a PMC floor that holds the SoC rail at its
highest state and give it to the decoder and the encoder as their
"perf" power domain. Each holds it only while it is runtime-active.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 76e0f6d5c3..63797d1fd6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -937,6 +937,9 @@ &dart_ave1 {
  * m1n1 hands over (CRCs, DART mappings) and never starts the coprocessor.
  */
 &ave {
+	power-domains = <&ps_venc_dma>, <&ps_venc_pipe4>, <&ps_venc_pipe5>,
+			<&ps_venc_me0>, <&ps_venc_me1>, <&pmc_soc_max>;
+	power-domain-names = "dma", "pipe4", "pipe5", "me0", "me1", "perf";
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -1434,6 +1437,23 @@ pmc_disp0: interface-disp0 {
 		apple,bwr-bit = <0x00>;
 		apple,boost-bit = <0x00>;
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The SoC rail at its highest state, 3 (the CLPC's T8132 table votes
+	 * no higher). The video decoder and encoder run at about half speed
+	 * below it, and nothing else raises the rail while they work.
+	 */
+	pmc_soc_max: floor-soc-max {
+		label = "soc-max";
+		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+		apple,rail = <1>;
+		apple,level = <3>;
+	};
+};
+
+&avd {
+	power-domains = <&ps_avd_sys>, <&pmc_soc_max>;
+	power-domain-names = "core", "perf";
 };
 
 &pmc_dispext0 {
-- 
2.43.0

